        model_answer="The two sides of the coil, P and Q, carry current in opposite directions as they pass through the field. By Fleming's left-hand rule each side experiences a force, and because the currents are opposite the forces are in opposite directions: one side is pushed up and the other down. These two forces act on opposite sides of the coil's axis, so together they produce a turning effect that rotates the coil.",
